 them I would just like to  say to everybody but it's been my honor  to serve for the last five years and I  hope that I've served my constituents  without asking them what their political  views are without judging people because  elections are one thing the duty and  responsibility of being an MP is quite  something else and it would be  it's my proud honor to can hope to  continue doing that for the next five  years but I would say ladies and  gentlemen having watched television this  evening it is a very good very good  result not only for myself here in  Watford but for David Cameron and I look  forward thank you I look forward to all  of the benefits that the last government  has brought to the Watford area to be  continued and I'll do my absolute best  to make sure that Watford continues to  thrive and prosper under a Conservative  government thank you very much indeed
 

